[Music]  my name is maya gray and i have a  youtube channel where i express my  creativity and show the love for my  dolls i'm going to be walking you guys  through on how i restored this bratz  campfire felicia doll felicia is from  the campfire line that bratz released in  2005 even though she was very underrated  when she first came out she quickly  became one of the most sought after  dolls to this day felicia pretty much  came with her full outfit she came with  a haircut a missing left brow and lip  chips and she also came with marks on  her body which looked like pens or like  crayons  i'm going to be undressing the doll just  to make it easier for me and just to  wash the clothes as well since they came  very dirty  i'm going to be taking her head off  which is going to help me with cutting  her hair removing what's inside as well  her hair came very chopped it was cut  short i'm just going to be using some  scissors to cut her hair and you want to  make sure that you're cutting down to  the roots pretty much just to get rid of  it and have a clean slate for the new  re-rooted hair  i'm going to be putting her hair into  boiling hot water and this will soften  up her vinyl like the plastic the head  to make it easier for you to plug the  hair out and it also does soften the  glue inside the head  i'm going to be using pointy tweezers to  pretty much pick out the remaining hair  that's inside the head just to make it  cleaner and easier for the reroute and  there's no remaining hair that's going  to be poking out with all of her new  hair  rerouting is pretty much replacing all  of her hair that's already rooted  i'm going to be using saran hair which  is pretty much the same as her factory  hair that she came with and i also  picked out the most similar colors that  i could find just to match it all  exactly  so using a rubric tool i'm going to be  poking each hair into the head pretty  much exactly how they did it in the  factory  i used the base of an exacto knife a  needle and i have a pick to help me out  poke holes into the doll just to make it  easier for the needle and it will also  save you some needles because it will  break if the hole isn't big enough or  the plastic has hardened so starting off  with the reroute i just sectioned out  some hair to make it easier for me  each strand of hair i pretty much wrap  around my finger  i use that to guide the needle and guide  the hair into the needle i used my pick  to create the bigger hole into the  doll's head and then after that i used  my re-rooting tool to insert the hair  into the doll's head  some of the existing holes might be  already  too big or like already cracked so if  you're using a pick to widen up the  holes just be careful just in case you  might crack a big hole into her head or  crack the plastic even more  so the doll came with some pen marks all  over her body  i'm going to be using some alcohol since  it kind of stained the plastic  she came with chip brows and chip lips  i'm just going to be repainting them  using some acrylic paint and some nail  polish that i have i just use a normal  paint brush typically used for doll  repaints and these are like usually  smaller than normal paint brushes since  it's for detailing  during repainting it's important to have  a steady hand  if there's any mistakes that i've done  with the repainting  i'm going to be using some rubbing  alcohol just to remove some of the  imperfections or like just to clean up  the repainting just a little bit just to  make her eyebrow  more sharp  so with repainting her lips i used nail  polish that was pretty much  clear and i used some eyeshadow that was  pretty similar to her lip color that i  found so it was pretty lucky so i just  mixed the clear nail polish and the  eyeshadow together just to have a paint  consistency  and i just used that to repaint her lips  i pretty much just used a normal washing  detergent for her clothes and used it  with some lukewarm water so i pretty  much just kind of scrunch it up in the  water just making sure all the dirt is  out of it  you can see by the water how dirty the  clothes came in so it was definitely a  good decision to wash them  [Music]  i'm going to be redressing her back into  the clothes that she came with  they are the original clothes from the  campfire line just some pieces missing  [Music]  i'm very happy with this restoration and  i'm happy to have felicia in my dog  collection since she is very sought  after and very loved by a lot of  collectors

